{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"for f in /workspace/requirements/*.yaml; do printf '--- %s ---\\\\n' \\\"\"'$f\"; sed -n '\"'1,240p' \\\"\"'$f\"; printf '\"'\\\\n'; done\"","aggregated_output":"/bin/bash: line 1: printf: --: invalid option\nprintf: usage: printf [-v var] format [arguments]\nid: \"lab1\"\ntitle: \"Lab 1 — Basic 5-Stage In-Order Pipeline\"\ncategory: systems\nrequirement: |-\n  ## Module: Lab 1 — Basic 5-Stage In-Order Pipeline\n\n  Implement the hollowed-out modules under `src/lab1/`. Classic IF→ID→EX→MEM→WB RV32I\n  pipeline. The ID stage resolves branches and contains forwarding muxes.\n\n  Modules to implement:\n  - **ALU** (`core/ALU.v`): 12-operation ALU (ADD, SUB, AND, OR, XOR, SLL, SRL, SRA, SLT,\n    SLTU, A+4, B-passthrough) with zero and overflow flags.\n  - **ImmGen** (`core/ImmGen.v`): Sign-extend immediates for I/B/J/S/U formats.\n  - **RAM_B** (`core/RAM_B.v`): Byte-addressable data memory with byte/half/word access.\n  - **Regs** (`core/Regs.v`): 31-entry register file with write-through, dual read ports.\n  - **REG_IF_ID** (`core/REG_IF_ID.v`): IF/ID latch with stall and flush support.\n  - **REG_ID_EX** (`core/REG_ID_EX.v`): ID/EX latch with flush-on-hazard support.\n  - **REG_EX_MEM** (`core/REG_EX_MEM.v`): EX/MEM pipeline register.\n  - **REG_MEM_WB** (`core/REG_MEM_WB.v`): MEM/WB pipeline register.\n  - **cmp_32** (`common/cmp_32.v`): 6-mode comparator (EQ, NE, LT, LTU, GE, GEU).\n  - **CtrlUnit** (`core/CtrlUnit.v`): Full RV32I control signal generation.\n  - **HazardDetectionUnit** (`core/HazardDetectionUnit.v`): Forwarding and stall logic.\n  - **RV32core** (`core/RV32core.v`): Top-level MUX wiring (PC select, forwarding, ALU inputs).\n\n  ## Files to modify\n  src/lab1/\n\n/bin/bash: line 1: printf: --: invalid option\nprintf: usage: printf [-v var] format [arguments]\nid: \"lab2\"\ntitle: \"Lab 2 — Pipeline with CSR and Exception Handling\"\ncategory: systems\nrequirement: |-\n  ## Module: Lab 2 — Pipeline with CSR and Exception Handling\n\n  Implement the hollowed-out modules under `src/lab2/`. Extends the Lab 1 5-stage pipeline\n  with M-mode CSR registers and a dedicated ExceptionUnit. CSRRegs implements CSRRW/CSRRS/CSRRC.\n  ExceptionUnit monitors instruction-level faults and triggers a PC redirect that flushes all\n  in-flight stages. All lab1-equivalent modules are re-implemented here with CSR/exception\n  signal extensions; the EX/MEM latch carries CSR and exception signals; RV32core adds the\n  exception redirect mux and cancel signals for suppressing register and memory writes on\n  faulted instructions.\n\n  Modules to implement (additions on top of the lab1 set):\n  - **CSRRegs** (`core/CSRRegs.v`): CSR register file supporting CSRRW/CSRRS/CSRRC.\n  - **ExceptionUnit** (`core/ExceptionUnit.v`): Exception handling with PC redirect.\n  - All lab1-equivalent modules (ALU, CtrlUnit, HazardDetectionUnit, ImmGen, Regs, RAM_B,\n    pipeline registers, RV32core) with CSR/exception extensions.\n\n  ## Files to modify\n  src/lab2/\n\n/bin/bash: line 1: printf: --: invalid option\nprintf: usage: printf [-v var] format [arguments]\nid: \"lab3\"\ntitle: \"Lab 3 — Pipeline with UART Simulation and Extended Hazards\"\ncategory: systems\nrequirement: |-\n  ## Module: Lab 3 — Pipeline with UART Simulation and Extended Hazards\n\n  Implement the hollowed-out modules under `src/lab3/`. A standalone 5-stage RV32I pipeline\n  variant built on the same module set as Lab 1. RAM_B adds simulated UART output: word\n  stores to address 0x10000000 print the ASCII character of the lower byte. CtrlUnit emits\n  CSR read/write control signals and a 2-bit exception vector. HazardDetectionUnit is\n  extended to handle the broader control signal set. All modules (ALU, ImmGen, Regs,\n  pipeline registers, CtrlUnit, HazardDetectionUnit, cmp_32, RV32core) are re-implemented\n  independently from lab1 and lab2.\n\n  ## Files to modify\n  src/lab3/\n\n/bin/bash: line 1: printf: --: invalid option\nprintf: usage: printf [-v var] format [arguments]\nid: \"lab4\"\ntitle: \"Lab 4 — In-Order Pipeline Variant with Cache Hierarchy\"\ncategory: systems\nrequirement: |-\n  ## Module: Lab 4 — In-Order Pipeline Variant with Cache Hierarchy\n\n  Implement the hollowed-out modules under `src/lab4/`. A 5-stage RV32I pipeline variant\n  that replaces the direct RAM_B connection with a two-level memory hierarchy: a Cache\n  Management Unit (CMU, pre-provided) sits between the MEM stage and a separate `data_ram`\n  module. The CMU introduces a `cmu_stall` signal that HazardDetectionUnit must propagate\n  to freeze the pipeline on cache misses. All core pipeline modules (ALU, ImmGen, Regs,\n  pipeline latches, CtrlUnit, HazardDetectionUnit, RV32core) use a different control signal\n  encoding than other labs.\n\n  ## Files to modify\n  src/lab4/\n\n/bin/bash: line 1: printf: --: invalid option\nprintf: usage: printf [-v var] format [arguments]\nid: \"lab5\"\ntitle: \"Lab 5 — Out-of-Order Execution with Scoreboard\"\ncategory: systems\nrequirement: |-\n  ## Module: Lab 5 — Out-of-Order Execution with Scoreboard\n\n  Implement the hollowed-out modules under `src/lab5/`. Replaces the in-order pipeline with\n  a scoreboard-based out-of-order execution engine. Pipeline stages: IF → Issue → Read\n  Operands → Execute (parallel FUs) → Write-Back. The scoreboard, CtrlUnit, RV32core, Regs,\n  and ImmGen are pre-provided; only the five FU modules require implementation.\n\n  Modules to implement:\n  - **FU_ALU** (`core/FU_ALU.v`): Stateful ALU FU — latches inputs on EN, produces result\n    in one cycle. Must implement state machine and full ALU computation.\n  - **FU_mul** (`core/FU_mul.v`): Multiplier FU with 64-cycle latency (shifting state register).\n    Instantiate `multiplier` IP, return lower 32 bits.\n  - **FU_div** (`core/FU_div.v`): Divider FU using AXI handshaking (valid/ready/data).\n    Instantiate `divider` IP, return quotient from upper 32 bits.\n  - **FU_jump** (`core/FU_jump.v`): Jump/branch FU — compare operands with `cmp_32`,\n    compute target PC = (JALR ? rs1 : PC) + imm, return address = PC + 4.\n  - **FU_mem** (`core/FU_mem.v`): Memory FU with 2-cycle latency. Compute address via\n    `add_32`, instantiate `RAM_B` for memory access.\n\n  ## Files to modify\n  src/lab5/\n\n/bin/bash: line 1: printf: --: invalid option\nprintf: usage: printf [-v var] format [arguments]\nid: \"lab6\"\ntitle: \"Lab 6 — Out-of-Order Execution with Tomasulo Algorithm\"\ncategory: systems\nrequirement: |-\n  ## Module: Lab 6 — Out-of-Order Execution with Tomasulo Algorithm\n\n  Implement the hollowed-out modules under `src/lab6/`. Full Tomasulo out-of-order execution\n  with reservation stations (RS), a Common Data Bus (CDB) broadcast, and a Register Alias\n  Table (RAT) integrated into the register file. Regs implements the RAT array\n  (`rs_num_A`/`rs_num_B` tag lookups) and CDB broadcast writeback. CtrlUnit is extended with\n  FU routing signals. The five FU modules share the same interface as Lab 5. RV32core wires\n  up RS modules per FU, manages PC/issue stall logic, selects the CDB source among finishing\n  FUs, and drives `wb_addr`/`wb_data` for test monitors. Lab 6 verification also re-runs\n  Lab 3's test program (`lab3_rom.mem`/`lab3_ram.mem`).\n\n  Modules to implement:\n  - **FU_ALU/FU_mul/FU_div/FU_jump/FU_mem**: Same functional units as lab5.\n  - **CtrlUnit** (`core/CtrlUnit.v`): Instruction decode with FU routing and op encoding.\n  - **Regs** (`core/Regs.v`): Register file with RAT for Tomasulo. Implement\n    `rs_num_A`/`rs_num_B` RAT lookups and CDB broadcast writeback.\n  - **RAM_B** (`core/RAM_B.v`): Extended RAM with UART simulation and larger address space.\n  - **ImmGen** (`core/ImmGen.v`): Immediate generator (same as other labs).\n  - **RV32core** (`core/RV32core.v`): Top-level wiring for Tomasulo — PC enable, issue enable,\n    RS allocation, reservation station port connections, FU port connections, CDB broadcast,\n    and stall logic.\n\n  ## Files to modify\n  src/lab6/\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
